            "review_title": "Review at Saigon Ngon Kitchen",
            "review_text": "Deborah Y\nRochdale, United Kingdom132 contributions\n0\nLovely food & cheap beer\nJan 2018\nWe stumbled across this place last night whilst out for a walk and found it really cheap in comparison to the bars on walking street. The staff are really friendly. It is very basic but in an ideal spot for people watching. We came in again this afternoon as we have an early bus to catch in the morning and decided to try the food. I had the fried rice with beef, shrimp and vegetables and my boyfriend had beef with pepper sauce & rice and both were really tasty and plentiful. The meals were 105k & 115k so for Uk standards we both found these to be reasonable prices. The bottles of Tiger are serviced ice cold and are 22k & 30k which is really good for this area I feel. On the whole I would recommend it. We are back from Mui Ne next week just for an overnight stay before we leave and will be back here for sure.\nRead more\nWritten January 4, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
